STORAGE: state state_rhs

SCHEDULE TestCarpetXAPI_Startup AT startup
{
  LANG: C
  OPTIONS: meta
} "Call CarpetX::active_window outside any traversal when TestCarpetXAPI::mode says so"

SCHEDULE TestCarpetXAPI_Register AT wragh
{
  LANG: C
  OPTIONS: global
} "Register a time integrator through CarpetX::register_integrator as TestCarpetXAPI::mode says"

SCHEDULE TestCarpetXAPI_ParamCheck AT paramcheck
{
  LANG: C
  OPTIONS: global
} "Register a time integrator after the driver has frozen its integrator record when TestCarpetXAPI::mode says so"

SCHEDULE TestCarpetXAPI_Fill AT initial
{
  LANG: C
  OPTIONS: global
} "Fill state through the public CarpetX API as TestCarpetXAPI::mode says"

SCHEDULE GROUP TestCarpetXAPI_CheckGroup AT initial AFTER TestCarpetXAPI_Fill
{
} "Check state after TestCarpetXAPI_Fill; TestCarpetXAPI_Fill traverses this group through CarpetX::run_schedule_group_at while a write scope on state is open when TestCarpetXAPI::mode says so"

SCHEDULE TestCarpetXAPI_Check IN TestCarpetXAPI_CheckGroup
{
  LANG: C
  READS: state(everywhere)
} "Abort unless state holds the written function everywhere, ghosts included"

SCHEDULE TestCarpetXAPI_SteerFirst AT initial AFTER TestCarpetXAPI_CheckGroup
{
  LANG: C
  OPTIONS: global
} "Steer CarpetX::poison_undefined_values to yes, open a write scope on state that promises the interior, then traverse TestCarpetXAPI_SteerNested through CarpetX::run_schedule_group_at, when TestCarpetXAPI::mode says so"

SCHEDULE GROUP TestCarpetXAPI_SteerNested
{
} "Traversed only by TestCarpetXAPI_SteerFirst, inside the scheduled routine that steered CarpetX::poison_undefined_values"

SCHEDULE TestCarpetXAPI_SteerInner IN TestCarpetXAPI_SteerNested
{
  LANG: C
  OPTIONS: global
} "Open a write scope on state that promises the interior inside TestCarpetXAPI_SteerFirst, when TestCarpetXAPI::mode says so"

SCHEDULE TestCarpetXAPI_SteerSecond AT initial AFTER TestCarpetXAPI_SteerFirst
{
  LANG: C
  OPTIONS: global
} "Open a write scope on state that promises the interior in the scheduled routine after TestCarpetXAPI_SteerFirst, then sync state, when TestCarpetXAPI::mode says so"

SCHEDULE TestCarpetXAPI_Step AT evol
{
  LANG: C
  OPTIONS: level
} "Run an RK step on state through CarpetX::open_rk_step on the levels being stepped, or skip it, as TestCarpetXAPI::mode says"

SCHEDULE TestCarpetXAPI_AfterShutdown AT shutdown AFTER Driver_Shutdown
{
  LANG: C
  OPTIONS: meta
} "Call CarpetX::num_levels after the driver has destroyed the grid hierarchy when TestCarpetXAPI::mode says so"
